/E (For Question 2, the methodology begins by initializing key parameters such as the universal gas constant \(R\) and specific heat capacities at constant volume \(Cv\) and constant pressure \(Cp\). The initial and intermediate states, characterized by temperatures \(T1_Q2, T2_Q2, T3_Q2\) and pressures \(P1_Q2, P2_Q2\), are defined. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
