/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (In the first process \(a\) of adiabatic compression, the work done, heat transfer, changes in internal energy, and enthalpy alterations are computed. Subsequently, in process \(b\) involving constant pressure cooling, similar calculations are performed to determine the work done, heat transfer, and changes in internal energy and enthalpy. The final process \(c\) revolves around isothermal expansion, where the associated thermodynamic parameters are evaluated. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
